The .svg files in this directory are unmodified Material Symbols (outlined, weight 400),
retrieved from https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@material-symbols/svg-400/outlined/.

Why they are vendored
---------------------
Talksmith fetches icons by name at render time, so a deck pulls only the handful it uses.
That works until there is no network and no warm cache — and then a deck that promised
semantic icons rendered a placeholder shape instead. This curated subset is the offline
floor: it covers the offline seed map, the neutral fallback chain, and the concepts that
show up in most decks, so `html-strict` always produces real glyphs.

It is deliberately a subset, not the library. An online render still resolves any icon in
the full Material Symbols catalog; these files are consulted only after the cache and the
network have both come up empty.

To add one: python3 skills/md-to-deck/icon_fetch.py <name> --cache skills/md-to-deck/icons
